findings.body:
**A symlinked skill directory named `*.md` skips the name check**

The gate checks a path's mode (refusing a symlink or gitlink) only for a path that `isSkillManifest` matches:

```ts
const isMisnamed = (path: string): boolean => {
  if (readFile === undefined || !isSkillManifest(path)) return false;
  const content = readFile(path);
  return content === null || (content !== undefined && isMisnamedSkill(path, content));
};
```

The exception `.claude/skills/**/*.md` compiles to `^\.claude/skills/(?:[^/]+/)*[^/]*\.md$`, so it also lifts a single entry `.claude/skills/shadow.md`. Take a branch scoped `.claude/skills/**` plus `docs/**` that adds two things:

- `.claude/skills/shadow.md`, a symlink (mode 120000) to `../../docs/shadow`
- `docs/shadow/SKILL.md`, with `name: pr-ci-review`

Here is what the gate does with them:

- `shadow.md` is lifted and in scope, and `isSkillManifest` is false for it. So `branchBlobReader` is never called and its mode-120000 refusal never runs.
- `docs/shadow/SKILL.md` is outside `.claude/skills/`, so nothing reads it.
- `refuseEscapingLinks` keeps the link because its target resolves inside the checkout.

After the merge, Claude Code lists `.claude/skills/` and can follow `shadow.md` to the directory. It then registers a skill named `pr-ci-review` from frontmatter the gate never read. ADR 0208 refuses a symlinked `SKILL.md` for exactly this reason ("a symlink would have Claude Code load its target's frontmatter"); this case is the same thing one level up. Whether Claude Code follows a symlinked directory entry can't be checked in-tree, hence medium confidence. No test covers a symlinked directory.

**Fix:** read every path the exception lifts, not only manifests. A null read is then refused anywhere under the exception. `isMisnamedSkill` already returns false for a path that is not a manifest, and a deleted path returns `undefined` and still passes.

<https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/77c0dfe4ff4f3bcc6a48d74abbd91e8262957f48/src/core/scope-audit.utils.ts#L45-L49>

findings.suggestion:
const isMisnamed = (path: string): boolean => {
  if (readFile === undefined || !exceptionRes.some((re) => re.test(path))) return false;
  const content = readFile(path);
  return content === null || (content !== undefined && isMisnamedSkill(path, content));
};

const block = FRONTMATTER.exec(content);
if (block === null) return FRONTMATTER_OPENING.test(content);
if (block[1]?.includes('---')) return true;
